  "interpretation": "Two focused one-boot A/B comparisons failed when the host sent serial log-read commands during RPC and passed when those commands were deferred. A full original native ALL run also passed when host polling was deferred past the signal and local-network benchmarks, whereas earlier active-polling full runs missed RPC/UDP. The evidence supports serial management activity as a material timing perturbation, but does not prove it is the only cause of all RPC timeouts or that the kernel is immune to other concurrent workloads."
